 "version": {
  "major": 1,
  "minor": 0
 },
 "description": "Boss DS-1 Distortion (1978) as Aion FX's Comet (document 1.1.0), the dual op-amp circuit with Aion's pre-1994 values and true bypass: an input buffer, a transistor booster (the Big Muff's first stage), an op-amp gain stage set by Distortion, two diodes clipping to VB, the Big Muff-style Tone, Level and an output buffer. Aion's Mode switch picks the diodes (the stock DS-1's), red LEDs, or two diodes each way. 2N5088s as Aion's substitute for the 2SC2248; the NJM3404A in Aion's kit, our card from Nisshinbo's sheet.",
 "tags": [
  "distortion"
 ],
 "starter": true,
 "power": {
  "rails": {
   "V+": 9.0
  }
 },
