   ]
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  {
   "title": "Try: later DS-1 values",
   "text": "Later (1994 on) DS-1 values: C5 68n, C6 100p, C7 470n; bass drops and treble rises a little at high Distortion. (idea from Aion FX's Comet notes)"
  },
  {
   "title": "Try: Big Muff-style clipping in Q2's stage",
   "text": "Q2's stage clips like a Big Muff's with 1N914s as D2 and D3 and 100n as C4 across R5 (the DS-1 has none). (idea from Aion FX's Comet notes)"
  },
  {
   "title": "Try: other op-amps for IC1",
   "text": "IC1: the kit's NJM3404AD (drawn), an LM358 relative. An NJM4580 or OPA2134 needs D4 out and a 1N914 as D11, anode to pin 6, cathode to pin 5. (idea from Aion FX's Comet notes)"
  },
  {
   "title": "Try: BAT46s in Mode up",
   "text": "Mode up: BAT46s as D6 and D8 clip near 1 V. (idea from Aion FX's Comet notes)"
  },
  {
   "title": "Try: known mods",
   "text": "Known mods (Keeley, Analogman): C10 47n softens the top end; R11 2k2 gives Distortion twice the range. (idea from Aion FX's Comet notes)"
  }
 ],
 "probes": {
  "in": "in",
  "out": "out"
 },
 "net_notes": {
  "clip": "The clipping node: the signal after the diodes, into the tone stack."
 },
